<html><head><title>What</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><img id="imagen" src="2_Researcher_files/researchertrail02.jpg" width="90%" onerror="this.style.display='none'" style="display: none;">                                                                    <h3 style="margin-top:14.05pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:14.05pt;
margin-left:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;color:windowtext;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">WHAT</span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
color:windowtext;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></h3><h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 12px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: Roboto, sans-serif;">

<p class="MsoNormal" style="font-weight: 600; margin: 12pt 0cm;"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Transdisciplinarity: Embracing Collaboration,
Tackling Challenges, and Cultivating Equality</span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 116%; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Transdisciplinary education has various
definitions, but they all agree on one thing: the nature of collaboration.
Academic, educational, and non-educational partners join forces in learning,
working, and researching.</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 116%; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-US">Participants are united by the central problem
or challenge. Transdisciplinarity is focused on engaging with complex societal
or sustainability issues that lack clear solutions and methods.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-US">A third characteristic of transdisciplinarity is
the form of involvement. In transdisciplinary teams, all partners work together
on an equal footing. Relationships can't be defined too rigidly because
everyone must learn together to develop new knowledge and innovative ideas and
take on various roles during the process. Hence, it is said that "there
are no transdisciplinary experts, only transdisciplinary practitioners."<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">These characteristics pose challenges,
especially from a researcher's perspective, who typically works as an expert in
a specific field. And: how do educational and research logics relate to each
other? TRAIL provides diverse insights and guidelines to help you tackle these
challenges.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><b>Inter- or Transdisciplinary: Common Confusions</b></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-US">Literature and experts emphasize that the
concept of transdisciplinarity is not always clearly defined (Klein, 2017). The
distinction between trans- and interdisciplinary collaboration is often
unclear. Both approaches aim for the integration of various types of knowledge.
Transdisciplinarity distinguishes itself by involving non-academic stakeholders
as equal participants in the collaboration. Therefore, transdisciplinarity
encompasses a greater diversity of perspectives and types of knowledge. As
complexity increases, so do the challenges and opportunities for learning and
new knowledge development.</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;
line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 116%; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p></h2>                                          </body></html>